# direnv entry point — auto-activates the Nix devShell on `cd`.
#
# One-time setup per developer:
#   1. Install direnv (https://direnv.net) and hook it into your shell.
#   2. (Recommended) Install nix-direnv for fast, cached shell entry:
#        https://github.com/nix-community/nix-direnv
#   3. Run `direnv allow` in this directory once.
#
# Not using direnv? Just run `nix develop` manually — same result.
use flake

# NVIM_LANGS (tells nvim's environment profile — files/nvim/lua/config/
# profile.lua — to load the dotnet feature: easy-dotnet/Roslyn LSP, Razor
# support, snippets) deliberately does NOT live here. .envrc is the
# shared/tracked project entry point; which editor features *you* load is a
# personal-machine concern. It's set in ./.dev.local.sh instead (gitignored,
# per-developer — auto-created by devshell-init from .dev.local.sh.example).
